# Hand one robot another robot's map, to be fused into what it knows.
#
# This is the physical half of a map exchange; the epistemic half is the
# announcement the executor applies to the model once the exchange completes.
# The reply says what the exchange actually carried, because a model that is
# told "the carrier now knows the bay is shut" should be checkable against a
# map in which the carrier can see the load.
#
# The map must be on the receiver's grid: same width, height, resolution and
# origin. The receiver refuses one that is not, for the reason
# epistemic_slam::fuse refuses it: a registration nobody performed is a merged
# map that is confidently wrong.

nav_msgs/OccupancyGrid map

# Who the map came from. Recorded, and used in the log line; the fusion itself
# does not depend on it.
string source

---

bool ok
string message

# Cells the receiver had not observed and now holds, over the whole grid.
uint32 newly_known

# The same, counted inside each named region the receiver watches, in the order
# of `regions`.
string[] regions
uint32[] newly_known_in_region

# Cells the two maps disagree about, free against occupied.
uint32 conflicts
